            [
              "Fetches",
              "one",
              "two"
            ],
            [
              "Config/hooks",
              "shared",
              "isolated"
            ],
            [
              "Pick when",
              "cheap parallel",
              "tool edits config"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Not storage",
          "text": "Stash as long-term storage is an anti-pattern. Anything you would be sad to lose belongs on a branch."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Time Cost"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Operation",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "stash push/pop",
              "diff size + tree write"
            ],
            [
              "worktree add",
              "checkout I/O only"
            ],
            [
              "full clone",
              "whole object db"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Stash is effectively instant on typical diffs",
            "Worktree add copies no objects, just admin bytes",
            "A 2 GB `.git` clone becomes 4 GB on disk"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Mental Cost"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An unlabeled stash stack is opaque",
            "Entries carry no branch context at all",
            "Worktrees: many dirs, each indexed by your IDE",
            "Tooling assuming one checkout misbehaves"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "gc roots",
          "text": "`git gc` runs on the shared object store, so it must treat every worktree's HEAD and index as roots. Prune before gc."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two worktrees run `status` and builds at once",
            "One working tree cannot",
            "Some ops still lock shared refs repo-wide"
          ]
        }
      ]
