      "page_title": "Storage, Scaling & Stash Slips",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Storage Cost"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One commit + trees + blobs per stash entry",
            "Deduplicated against existing objects — cheap",
            "Unless `-a` swallowed your build output",
            "`clone --shared`/`--reference` skips the copy",
            "But leaves a fragile link to the source repo"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How Each Scales",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Count",
            "Stash",
            "Worktrees"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1-2",
              "fine",
              "fine"
            ],
            [
              "~5",
              "degrades",
              "fine"
            ],
            [
              ">5",
              "opaque stack",
              "disk + indexing"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stash Slips And Fixes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Slip",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "pop on a moved base",
              "git stash branch"
            ],
            [
              "No -u, then clean -fd",
              "nothing — gone"
            ],
            [
              "clear to 'tidy up'",
              "fsck, gc window"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The stash base commit differs, so the pop conflicts",
            "`git stash branch <name>` reapplies on that base",
            "Default to `git stash push -u` and stop losing files",
            "`clear` makes entries unreachable immediately"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Duplicate Loop"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Conflicted pop, resolve, commit — entry still there",
            "Later you pop it and reapply the same change",
            "Read `git stash list` right after resolving"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Triage A Rotting Stack"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git stash show -p stash@{3}",
            "git stash branch keep stash@{3}",
            "git stash drop stash@{3}"
          ],
          "note": "inspect before you trust an entry"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Promote anything you still want to a branch",
            "Drop the rest one by one, never `clear`",
            "Keep the stack under ==five== entries"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Two defaults",
          "text": "Always `-m` so entries stay readable, always `-u` so new files travel. Those two flags prevent most stash pain."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stashes Are Not Branch-Bound"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "It does not belong to the branch you made it on",
            "Read the 'WIP on <branch>' text before popping"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "$ git stash list",
            "stash@{0}: WIP on feature-a: 3f2a1 lexer",
            "stash@{1}: On main: wip: parser fix"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Worktree Slips, Decision Table & Cheat Sheet",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worktree Slips And Fixes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Slip",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "rm -rf the directory",
              "git worktree prune"
            ],
            [
              "add on live branch",
              "--detach or new br"
